   "answer": "For a cabinet, you're probably looking for a cabinet turntable (Lazy Susan) — a rotating platform that lets you easily access items stored inside a cabinet.\n\nThere are three common types:\n\nShop\n\n1. Round cabinet turntable\n\nSits on an existing shelf and rotates 360°. Great for spices, bottles, and pantry items. Usually requires no installation.\n\nShop\n\n2. Corner cabinet Lazy Susan\n\nBuilt into corner cabinets, often with two rotating shelves. Makes hard-to-reach storage accessible.\n\nShop\n\n3. Turntable bearing hardware\n\nA metal rotating mechanism for DIY cabinet shelves or rotating platforms.\n\nSome options to buy\n\nOXO 11-In Round Lazy Susan Turntable, White\n\n$15.71\n\nDowell 2-Shelf Kidney Lazy Susan Corner Cabinet Organizer, 2…\n\n$109.99\n\nEverbilt 6 in. Square Lazy-Susan Turntable with 400 lb. Load…\n\n$7.87\n\nWhich kind are you looking for?\n\nA rotating organizer that sits inside a cabinet\nA built-in rotating shelf for a corner cabinet\nJust the rotating bearing hardware for a DIY project\nFind matching turntables"
